crates/arbor-gui/src/app_bootstrap.rs:459:1: [GPUI-01-Lifecycle] App entry point — Application::new().run(|cx: &mut App|) starts the event loop, cx.open_window() creates a native window, cx.new(|cx| YourStruct) allocates the root entity
crates/arbor-gui/src/app_bootstrap.rs:478:1: [GPUI-02-Entity] cx.new(|cx| ...) — allocates an entity (GPUI's state container). Returns Entity<T>. The entity owns your struct and GPUI manages its lifetime. This is the GPUI equivalent of a React component instance.
crates/arbor-gui/src/rendering.rs:168:1: [GPUI-03-Render] impl Render for ArborWindow — GPUI's core trait. Called each frame (when cx.notify() fires). Returns impl IntoElement (an element tree). No virtual DOM — GPUI diffs the tree on the GPU.
crates/arbor-gui/src/rendering.rs:197:1: [GPUI-04-RootTree] The root element tree — div() chains with CSS-like flex. .size_full() .bg() .flex_col() build the layout. Read top-to-bottom: styling, event handlers, children, modals.
crates/arbor-gui/src/rendering.rs:233:1: [GPUI-05-Composition] .when(condition, |this| this.child(...)) — conditional rendering. Also: .when_some(option, |this, val|) for Option. .child() adds one child, .children() adds an iterator.
crates/arbor-gui/src/rendering.rs:329:1: [GPUI-06-Styling] Complete styling example — .px_6() .py_4() .rounded_lg() .bg() .border_1() .flex_col() .items_center() .gap_3(). CSS flexbox in Rust method chains. Values are multiples of 4px.
crates/arbor-gui/src/app_bootstrap.rs:38:1: [GPUI-07-Keybindings] cx.bind_keys() — maps key combos to action types globally. KeyBinding::new("cmd-t", SpawnTerminal, None). Third arg scopes to focus context (None = global).
crates/arbor-gui/src/rendering.rs:208:1: [GPUI-08-ActionDispatch] .on_action(cx.listener(Self::method)) — registers action handler on this element. Actions bubble UP from focused element. cx.listener() captures weak entity ref for the retained tree.
crates/arbor-gui/src/key_handling.rs:647:1: [GPUI-08-ActionHandler] Action handler signature: (&mut self, _: &ActionType, window: &mut Window, cx: &mut Context<Self>). Wired via .on_action(). The _ is common for zero-sized actions.
crates/arbor-gui/src/key_handling.rs:709:1: [GPUI-09-Notify] cx.notify() — GPUI's "setState". Tells GPUI to re-render this entity. WITHOUT this call, UI won't update after state changes. Explicit by design — no speculative re-renders.
crates/arbor-gui/src/welcome_ui.rs:176:1: [GPUI-10-Focus] Focus system — .track_focus(&handle) attaches, window.focus(&handle) sets focus. Unlike HTML, clicking does NOT auto-focus. You must call window.focus() yourself in on_mouse_down.
crates/arbor-gui/src/rendering.rs:206:1: [GPUI-11-Events] .on_key_down(cx.listener(Self::handle)) — type-safe event handlers. Also: on_click, on_mouse_down(MouseButton::Left, ...), on_mouse_move, on_drag_move. Closures get (event, window, cx).
crates/arbor-gui/src/version_check.rs:69:1: [GPUI-12-Async] The canonical async pattern: cx.spawn(|this, cx|) → cx.background_spawn(work).await → this.update(cx, |this, cx| { mutate; cx.notify(); }) → .detach(). Three layers: main thread / thread pool / entity update.
crates/arbor-gui/src/command_palette.rs:547:1: [GPUI-13-Modals] Modal pattern — store Option<State>, return div() when None. Open: set Some + notify. Close: set None + notify. Overlay: .absolute().inset_0() backdrop + centered content.
crates/arbor-gui/src/diff_view.rs:80:1: [GPUI-14-Lists] uniform_list(id, count, |range, _, _| render_visible_rows) — virtualized list, only renders on-screen rows. .track_scroll(handle) for programmatic scroll. "uniform" = same-height rows.
crates/arbor-gui/src/rendering.rs:308:1: [GPUI-FullExample] Quit dialog — complete mini-app showing every concept: .when() conditional, .absolute().inset_0() overlay, .bg().opacity() backdrop, .on_click() dismiss, flex centering, button styling
crates/arbor-gui/src/sidebar.rs:154:1: [GPUI-Bonus-Animation] with_animation((id, epoch), Animation::new(150ms).with_easing(ease_in_out), |el, delta| el.opacity(...)). delta goes 0→1. Change the ID to re-trigger.
crates/arbor-gui/src/terminal_rendering.rs:461:1: [GPUI-Canvas] canvas() — escape hatch to raw GPU painting. Two closures: prepaint (layout) and paint (draw). Inside paint: window.paint_quad() for rects, window.text_system().shape_line() for text.
crates/arbor-gui/src/diff_engine.rs:453:1: [GPUI-AsyncEntity] cx.spawn(async move |this, cx|) — entity-aware async. this is WeakEntity (won't keep entity alive). this.update(cx, |this, cx|) safely mutates. Returns Err if entity dropped.
crates/arbor-gui/src/github_service.rs:694:1: [GPUI-SmolTokio] Two async runtimes bridge — GPUI uses smol, octocrab needs tokio. Solution: short-lived tokio::runtime::Runtime for the API call. Common pattern when mixing runtime-locked libraries.
crates/arbor-gui/src/actions.rs:3:1: [GPUI-Actions] actions!() macro — generates zero-sized action types. Each action is a unique Rust type for compile-time event matching. No stringly-typed events.
crates/arbor-gui/src/actions.rs:29:1: [GPUI-ActionData] #[derive(gpui::Action)] — actions with data. ConnectToLanDaemon carries an index. Use #[action(namespace, no_json)] for non-serializable payloads.
crates/arbor-gui/src/rendering.rs:11:1: [GPUI-IME] EntityInputHandler — GPUI's Input Method Editor protocol. replace_text_in_range routes committed text to the right component (terminal, text field, etc.).
crates/arbor-terminal-emulator/src/alacritty_support.rs:26:1: [Alacritty] Terminal emulation without a window — Term (grid + state machine) + Processor (VTE parser). Feed bytes in, read styled cells out.
crates/arbor-terminal-emulator/src/alacritty_support.rs:69:1: [Alacritty] process_terminal_bytes — feeds raw bytes into VTE parser. Generation counter (AtomicU64) enables cache invalidation for snapshots.
crates/arbor-terminal-emulator/src/alacritty_support.rs:95:1: [Alacritty] EventListener — tap into terminal events (Bell, Title) via atomic counter. Lock-free observation pattern.
crates/arbor-mcp/src/lib.rs:284:1: [MCP] #[tool_handler] + ServerHandler — MCP protocol handshake. get_info() declares capabilities (tools, resources, prompts). Auto-registered via proc macros.
crates/arbor-mcp/src/lib.rs:356:1: [MCP] serve_stdio() — entire MCP server in 3 lines. ArborMcp::new().serve(rmcp::transport::io::stdio()).await. Runs over stdin/stdout for AI agent integration.
crates/arbor-mcp/src/tools.rs:139:1: [MCP] #[tool_router] + #[tool(description)] — auto-generates MCP tool definitions with JSON Schema from schemars derives. Zero manual schema writing.
crates/arbor-gui/src/diff_engine.rs:121:1: [imara-diff] Histogram diff — BlobInternedInput interns files to integers, BlobDiff::compute runs O(ND) on tokens. Same algorithm as git since 2.44.
crates/arbor-gui/src/terminal_backend.rs:93:1: [portable-pty] PTY lifecycle — openpty (master+slave pair), slave.spawn_command (shell), master.try_clone_reader/take_writer (I/O handles). Same mechanism as iTerm2/Alacritty.
crates/arbor-httpd/src/mdns.rs:24:1: [zeroconf] mDNS registration — _arbor._tcp with TXT records. Same protocol as AirPlay/Chromecast. Auto-discovers daemons on LAN.
crates/arbor-ssh/src/connection.rs:38:1: [libssh-rs] SSH connection — reads ~/.ssh/config, auth cascade (agent → auto key). ProcessConfig(true) enables Host aliases and ProxyJump.
crates/arbor-tui/src/capture.rs:3:1: [Trait design] TerminalCapture trait — pluggable terminal backends. capture_for() dispatcher reads metadata.terminal.type. Clean extension point.
crates/arbor-tui/src/main.rs:31:1: [ratatui] TUI event loop — enable_raw_mode, EnterAlternateScreen, terminal.draw(). Panic hook restores terminal state on crash.
